## High severity

### 1.1 Developer Sandbox reachable in production — ✅ Done
- **Problem:** `DeveloperSandboxSection` had no build check, so 7 taps on the Settings header in a store build exposed
  `clearAllData()` and `seedMockData()`.
- **Fix:** gated on the pure function `shouldShowDeveloperSandbox(devModeEnabled, isDebug, isTestFlight)`, unit-tested
  as a truth table (`DeveloperSandboxGateTest`).
- **Verified:** Pixel 9 debug shows the sandbox after 7 taps; release does not (after 7 or 14 taps).
- **Consequence:** a release-build R8/Crashlytics check can no longer use the 7-tap unlock. Use a debug or temporary
  local build (noted in `docs/Launch/06`).
- **Still open:** confirm on the next iOS TestFlight build that the sandbox appears after 7 taps.

### 1.2 Static callbacks in iOS Gemma installer — ✅ Done (iOS device check pending)
- **Problem:** `progressReporter`/`completionReporter` are static `var`s on the `companion object` of
  `GemmaBaseModelInstaller.ios.kt`. `PayslipViewModel` is a Koin `factory`, so each new instance overwrote the global
  listeners and orphaned the previous subscriber. In practice the ViewModel is resolved once per
  `makeUIViewController` (iOS) or `onCreate` (Android), so this was latent rather than observed.
- **Second bug found while reading the code:** the installer was never injected. `AppModule` called
  `PayslipViewModel(get(), get())`, so the installer came from the default argument `provideGemmaBaseModelInstaller()`
  and was a new instance per ViewModel. "Make it a `single`" therefore also needed a Koin registration and a third
  `get()`. Separately, `GemmaOnDemandResourceBridge.beginFetch()` replaces its `NSBundleResourceRequest` on every
  trigger, and `install()` runs from both ViewModel init and `resumeModelDownload()`. A double trigger could start a
  second request and drop the first, and ODR may purge a resource once no live request holds it.
- **Fix:** chose the Koin `single` over the listener registry, because the registry changes the companion API and so the
  Swift bridge (where the retain-cycle risk sat). The companion slots and `GemmaOnDemandResourceBridge.swift` are
  untouched.
  - `AppModule`: `single<GemmaBaseModelInstaller> { provideGemmaBaseModelInstaller() }` and
    `PayslipViewModel(get(), get(), get())`.
  - `IosGemmaBaseModelInstaller`: a `fetchInFlight` flag makes a second `install()` a no-op until the bridge reports
    completion. It is only set once `installTrigger` exists, so a missing bridge can never block a retry.
- **Tests:**
  - `GemmaInstallerDiWiringTest` (composeApp): two ViewModels resolved from `appModule` share one installer. Failed
    before the fix, passes after.
  - `IosGemmaBaseModelInstallerTest`: a second `install()` while a fetch is in flight does not re-trigger (red, then
    green); `install()` after a failed fetch does trigger again (green throughout; guards against the flag stranding
    the retry button).
- **Verified:** ktlint, tech-debt audit, `check` (incl. 52-fixture corpus), full `iosSimulatorArm64Test`, iOS framework
  link. `xcodebuild` was not run because no Swift or Xcode file changed.
- **Not verified:** a real ODR download on a device. Android now shares one installer too (the registration is in
  `commonMain`); from reading the code its lazy gateway registers its Play Core listener once per process instead of
  once per ViewModel, but that was not run on a device.
- **Debt left:** the statics remain, and `PayslipViewModel` keeps its `provideGemmaBaseModelInstaller()` default argument
  (tests rely on it), so any caller that builds a ViewModel outside Koin still gets a private installer that overwrites
  the shared reporters. A listener registry would be the fuller fix if more than one live subscriber is ever needed.

