## Low severity

### 3.1 Firebase anonymous auth and token bridge — ✅ Done
- **Problem:** left over from the Cloud Functions era. `AuthTokenProvider.getIdToken()` had zero production callers, yet
  iOS signed in anonymously on every launch (Android never did).
- **Fix:** removed the `auth/` classes (all three source sets) and their tests, the Swift sign-in and token bridge,
  `AuthTokenFetcherTests`, `firebase-auth-ktx`, both `FirebaseAuth` Xcode product refs, and the now-stale
  `SignInHubActivity` manifest removal. Firebase Core, Crashlytics and Analytics are unchanged.
- **Verified:** `check` (incl. 52-fixture corpus), iOS simulator tests, framework link, `assembleRelease`/R8,
  `xcodebuild` build + Swift unit tests. No `firebase-auth`/`play-services-auth`/`credentials` artifact remains in the
  release runtime classpath (only the unrelated `play-services-auth-blockstore`). Cold launch is clean on the Pixel 9
  (debug) and the iOS simulator.
- **Not verified:** Pixel release build on-device (needs an uninstall), and Crashlytics receiving events from the next
  TestFlight build. After older iOS builds age out, the Anonymous provider can be disabled in the Firebase console.

### 3.2 Unused Ktor `HttpClient` — ✅ Done
Deleted the `single { HttpClient … }` block. A follow-up (`5fded6b6`) removed the orphaned Ktor build dependencies and
catalog entries (release APK ~108 KB smaller). `-dontwarn io.ktor.**` is kept on purpose.

### 3.3 Dead `NetworkErrorMapper` — ✅ Done
Deleted with its test.

### 3.4 Deprecated `UploadWidget` — ✅ Done
Deleted with its test, along with three orphaned `AppStrings` constants. Docs now point to `ImportPayslipDialog`.

